Z||000002||NOS3800||10-01-2001||11:24 PM||||Thanks for the compliments. The color is derived from 97-98 Ford Probe/Mustang Purple. It is custom, we applied alittle more red pearl to the color. I believe it is called bright sapphire metallic. ITS EXPENSIVE. 60.00 for a 1/4 quart. Expect to pay 1600-2000 to have your car sprayed this color. There is a cheapy version that was applied to the escorts and rangers. It may be cheaper and looks very similar. Go to your local bodyshop and ask to look through their color chips. Its usually broken down by auto manufacturer.<BR>I am an autobody tech, and my brother is the painter at our bodyshop, so you do the math. ;^) I got my car painted for free, just had to pay for materials which was worked out with the owner by working on a minivan that was an all over as payment.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.45@101.12 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BillCar2001_4.jpg"> ||||reg||10
